## 9. Parallel Requests — `Promise.allSettled()`

Hospital and police searches are independent, so both run in parallel:

```javascript
const results = await Promise.allSettled([
  api.get("/maps/nearby", { params: { lat, lng, type: "healthcare.hospital" } }),
  api.get("/maps/nearby", { params: { lat, lng, type: "service.police" } })
]);
```

**Why not `Promise.all()`?** `Promise.all()` rejects the *entire* operation if even one request fails. `Promise.allSettled()` returns each result independently — a hospital failure won't hide a successful police result.

> **Interview answer:** I used Promise.allSettled because hospital and police searches are independent. A failure in one should not block the successful result of the other.

**Result handling:**
```javascript
// fulfilled
setNearbyHospitals(hospitalResult.value.data.places || []);
// rejected
setNearbyHospitals([]); // error logged, page keeps working
```
Same pattern applies to police results.

