## 13. First Aid Guide

**File:** `frontend/src/components/FirstAidGuide.jsx` (separated from `Emergency.jsx` for separation of concerns).

**Categories:**
- Common Emergencies (bleeding, cuts, burns, choking, CPR, fainting, shock)
- Injuries (sprains, fractures, head injuries, nosebleeds, eye injuries, bites)
- Travel Emergencies (heat exhaustion/stroke, dehydration, sunburn, hypothermia)
- Other (allergic reactions, electric shock, seizures)

> Basic guidance only — does not replace professional medical care.

**Data structure:**
```javascript
const firstAidData = [
  {
    title: "Burns",
    category: "Common Emergencies",
    steps: [
      "Move away from the heat source.",
      "Cool the area with cool running water.",
      "Do not apply ice directly.",
      "Seek medical help for serious burns."
    ]
  }
];
```

**Filtering:**
```javascript
firstAidData.filter(item => item.category === activeCategory);
```

**Why static?** First aid info is general, non-user-specific, and not trip-specific — so no API/DB call is needed. This is fast, easy to maintain, easy to cache, and sets up well for future offline support.

